WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:20.326
In the first season, you saw us setting up this tent,
 which was a massive&nbsp;upgrade back then.

00:00:20.326 --> 00:00:24.038
However, the tent started deteriorating massively over time.

00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:28.399
The&nbsp;canvas is falling apart and the frame is not sturdy at all.

00:00:28.399 --> 00:00:31.868
So, we will try to find&nbsp;a way to fix it in this episode.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:35.020
But first, we will harvest some vegetables at Nuno's&nbsp;farm.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.620
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:41.349 --> 00:00:44.785
- Today, some of us are heading over&nbsp;
to Nuno's farm to help with the&nbsp;harvesting.

00:00:45.127 --> 00:00:48.462
We're bringing some crates 
to collect our own fruit and vegetables.

00:01:03.457 --> 00:01:07.132
It's not the first time we've&nbsp;been here,
 but it's always nice&nbsp;to have a tour of the farm.

00:01:07.702 --> 00:01:09.810
So, first up: the animals.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.540
They are an important part of the farm,
as the manure is used as fertilizer.

00:01:26.706 --> 00:01:28.920
Welcome to Nuno's regenerative farm.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.390
Nuno, what kind of farm is this?

00:01:34.216 --> 00:01:37.301
- It's a wild farm of some kind.

00:01:37.301 --> 00:01:43.025
A mixed farm, between gardening, 
an orchard and a lot of different things.

00:01:43.025 --> 00:01:47.161
It's an&nbsp;ecological farm, because, yeah,
 we leave a space for everything.

00:01:47.161 --> 00:01:50.950
We have a pieces of soil digged...

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.889
We&nbsp;have grass...

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:54.879
We have dry things...

00:01:54.879 --> 00:01:59.593
We have three small shrubs, and a bit of everything!

00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:03.507
So, everyone finds a bit of food here.

00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:09.283
And then, we generate a harmony,
 where a lot of food remains&nbsp;for us still as well.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:13.840
- Nuno's goal is to create a farm as an ecosystem that is self-sustaining.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.065
Creating space for multiple types of vegetation, insects and wildlife.

00:02:18.065 --> 00:02:20.872
And therefore, creating a more&nbsp;resilient ecosystem.

00:02:20.872 --> 00:02:25.406
This is called regenerative farming, which we already saw in update 90.

00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:29.901
The&nbsp;principle is to create rich soil and diversify crops.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:33.815
So, there's no need for chemical inputs,
&nbsp;to fertilize and protect the plants from pests.

00:02:33.815 --> 00:02:36.839
We are excited to help out and learn from him!

00:02:38.121 --> 00:02:41.426
But, we came to help harvesting, so here we go.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:09.900
After a few hours of harvesting, we filled up&nbsp;the crates
 and we're ready to head back to Kamp.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.238
Nuno, are you happy with the harvesting help?

00:04:13.238 --> 00:04:14.683
- Yuuuup!

00:04:52.179 --> 00:04:53.471
Until next time!

00:04:57.187 --> 00:04:59.714
- After the harvest, we have a lot of tomatoes.

00:04:59.714 --> 00:05:02.807
We thought it would be good to make
&nbsp;some sauce for the pizza night.

00:05:02.807 --> 00:05:06.033
But first, we are going to renovate the tent.

00:05:06.821 --> 00:05:09.828
- So, here we are, underneath a white tent.

00:05:09.828 --> 00:05:14.184
You can see it is totally breaking down
 and we are doing a fix on it.

00:05:14.184 --> 00:05:17.636
This white&nbsp;tent has been here since
 the first season of Project Kamp.

00:05:17.636 --> 00:05:20.490
It has been giving a great service to the Kamp.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.476
So much that it becomes a very messy warehouse.

00:05:23.476 --> 00:05:28.341
On top of that, the biggest problem is&nbsp;the 
intense sun and rain that ruined the canvas.

00:05:28.683 --> 00:05:32.512
It has many holes and we already patched some of them.

00:05:32.512 --> 00:05:36.958
But, it's still very ripped, which also produce a lot of microplastics.

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:38.434
Not good for the environment!

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:41.008
Maybe not the best solution for the outdoor...

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:45.098
Besides that, the frame is getting wobbly and&nbsp;unstable.

00:05:45.098 --> 00:05:46.369
So, we need to fix that too.

00:05:46.711 --> 00:05:48.691
Before we start, we need a new tarp.

00:05:48.691 --> 00:05:53.364
So, Dave and Adrian went to&nbsp;a scrapyard,
to look for second-hand one.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.450
There's a lot to choose from,
 but it&nbsp;was hard to find one in good condition...

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.524
Finally, we found a blue tarp, which is very dirty,
but still in good shape.

00:06:21.524 --> 00:06:25.297
We put it&nbsp;in a pickup, and went back to Kamp.

00:06:41.253 --> 00:06:42.685
Now, we can start working!

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:52.448
So, on the tarp, we&nbsp;found a lot of these stainless steel brackets,
 which are still quite usable and quite strong!

00:06:52.448 --> 00:07:00.994
But, the thing is they are secure by 
a really rusty screw that is unscrewable...

00:07:00.994 --> 00:07:04.620
So, I guess that's we have to grind it out.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.900
This tarp actually comes with a&nbsp;lot of these roller metal parts.

00:07:37.213 --> 00:07:40.813
They need to be removed, before we can reuse them.

00:07:59.134 --> 00:08:00.612
- Is it complicated to take it out?

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:06.461
It's tricky, time-consuming and rusty, but doable.

00:08:08.202 --> 00:08:13.122
Now that the wheels and buckles&nbsp;are out, we can measure the top.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:34.970
After checking on the tarp, we&nbsp;found there are 
different part with damages.

00:08:35.768 --> 00:08:42.018
So, these are the&nbsp;areas that we will be avoiding.

00:08:59.421 --> 00:09:02.131
We did some measuring on&nbsp;the size of the tarp.

00:09:03.185 --> 00:09:09.796
It is 13 meters (≈ 43 feet) long, 
and around a 2.7 meters (≈ 9 feet) width.

00:09:11.205 --> 00:09:15.427
We are going to see how we are going to cut and use it.

00:09:15.427 --> 00:09:20.520
In order to do that, we need to&nbsp;clear the old white tent,
 so we can measure it too.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.780
Thanks Julie!

00:10:25.236 --> 00:10:27.396
Now, some last measurements.

00:10:37.047 --> 00:10:43.189
Now, we have measured the roof size, 
and now&nbsp;it's come to the cutting of the banner.

00:10:43.474 --> 00:10:44.340
Exciting!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:38.786
We have put the tarp onto the structure, 
but&nbsp;there's a lot of dirt on top of it.

00:11:38.786 --> 00:11:41.197
So, we decide we need to clean a little bit.

00:11:41.197 --> 00:11:45.000
Otherwise, we will worry&nbsp;that the mud will 
actually break the sewing machine...

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:15.960
With the material that big, it's very difficult&nbsp;
to push into the sewing machines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.684 --> 00:12:23.524
This is one attempt on rolling it both&nbsp;sides,
so it can enter the machine.

00:12:23.524 --> 00:12:30.275
We can do a stitch in the middle right here.

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:34.464
I'm not sure if it works, but we'll see!

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:43.231
So, because the material is super big,
 we need a&nbsp;big platform to put it on to do this sewing

00:12:43.981 --> 00:12:49.451
The only big and flat surface is the platform&nbsp;of the kitchen.

00:12:50.344 --> 00:12:51.746
Let's try to work in here!

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:25.783
So, now we have put a machine here,
 and the&nbsp;material is inside of the machine.

00:13:25.783 --> 00:13:28.500
Now, we try to sew...

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.340
I can't use the sewing machine in&nbsp;a proper way.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.696
The canvas is too big to push in.

00:14:14.696 --> 00:14:19.980
It's very thick, and I had to&nbsp;steer it by hand,
just so the needle won't break.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.820
This is the most frustrating&nbsp;moment in the whole season...

00:14:36.593 --> 00:14:42.574
So, we broke one needle already,
and we&nbsp;are now using our last needle.

00:14:42.574 --> 00:14:43.821
We only have two.

00:14:43.821 --> 00:14:46.722
If it breaks, we have to do hand stitching...

00:15:17.629 --> 00:15:23.100
We just did one stitch, and now we're going
 to&nbsp;turn it around and do another one.

00:15:32.683 --> 00:15:35.886
It is very difficult and exhausting work.

00:15:35.886 --> 00:15:39.780
It&nbsp;took us four hours just to sew six meters of tarp!

00:15:52.335 --> 00:15:58.020
The sewing machines appear to be 
really&nbsp;struggling on doing the second stitching.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.860
So, I think we need another approach... 

00:16:05.374 --> 00:16:08.591
Instead of sewing, we're now trying&nbsp;a different approach.

00:16:08.591 --> 00:16:17.344
Which is using rivet and putting a spacer underneath it,
to pull two layers of fabric together.

00:16:19.144 --> 00:16:20.460
Let's do it!

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:38.220
Phew! It works, and now we have a one big piece of fabric!

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:46.560
So, I guess this is time to say&nbsp;goodbye to the white fabric?

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.260
Now, we need&nbsp;something to attach it to the ground.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:21.030
So, these are two of the seat belt taken out from the yellow van.

00:17:22.027 --> 00:17:27.188
We're trying to take it apart, get the strap out, 
for trying to use it to strap down the tent.

00:17:27.188 --> 00:17:29.317
Let's see how it goes!

00:18:19.316 --> 00:18:20.886
Okay, so...

00:18:21.598 --> 00:18:29.332
We have cut this double-sided part,
 so&nbsp;we can use it as a strap to hold the tent down.

00:18:45.978 --> 00:18:52.608
We are making this little tap that goes&nbsp;underneath the top.

00:18:52.608 --> 00:18:56.574
For it to grab onto the metal frame.

00:18:56.574 --> 00:18:58.680
So, now, we are attaching it!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:12.840
Now that the tarp is attached to the frame,
it seems it will hold and not fly away.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.513
We hope so!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:21.391
So, now the almost final&nbsp;part is to add this strap onto the tarp.

00:19:21.391 --> 00:19:25.287
It will act as a pulling&nbsp;force, to hold the whole tent down.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:45.960
The last step will be putting on the legs 
and&nbsp;fasten the tent to the ground, just so it's tight.

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:17.520
With the buckles we got from&nbsp;the tarp, it is super easy to do!

00:20:29.646 --> 00:20:34.058
The last strap is down&nbsp;and it is done!

00:20:36.237 --> 00:20:38.007
- Nice work!

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.256
So, the old white tent is gone.

00:20:46.256 --> 00:20:48.358
It has been very&nbsp;useful for us.

00:20:48.358 --> 00:20:52.135
But, besides the structure, 
the fabric wasn't going to last much longer.

00:20:52.135 --> 00:20:55.560
Now, it&nbsp;seems like it has come back to life with this blue tarp!

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.815
The material is thick and resistant.

00:20:58.815 --> 00:21:01.990
It's&nbsp;quite difficult to work with, but we've managed with it.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.371
It feels like it's gonna last forever.

00:21:04.371 --> 00:21:09.547
We have&nbsp;some leftover material,
 so we can use it for the next project.

00:21:09.547 --> 00:21:10.932
Let's see!

00:21:10.932 --> 00:21:17.160
It is great to give&nbsp;a second life to this material,
although we have to throw away the white top.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:20.460
Even the&nbsp;old yellow van seat belts have a new use!

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:25.693
The space underneath is now empty and ready for new use.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.851
- A super cool tent!

00:21:28.851 --> 00:21:32.017
Now, we are going to the kitchen to make some tomato pulp.

00:21:32.017 --> 00:21:34.847
For that, we need Dorian.

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:38.580
- So, today we're making tomato pulp.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:42.496
We got these lovely tomatoes from Nuno's farm.

00:21:42.496 --> 00:21:45.660
And then, we have a&nbsp;lot of tomatoes for pizza night.

00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:58.380
So, now that we've boiled our tomatoes,
I'm gonna blend this with this mixer.

00:23:59.721 --> 00:24:02.592
The next step then would be to&nbsp;put it into the bottles.

00:24:02.592 --> 00:24:04.041
So, let's go!

00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:30.782
Now, I need to fill up the bottles, when the sauce&nbsp;is hot.

00:24:30.782 --> 00:24:35.837
Then, it cools down and creates a vacuum, 
so there's no more space for bacteria to grow&nbsp;inside.

00:24:35.837 --> 00:24:38.640
And, it stays good for a longer time!

00:24:56.640 --> 00:25:01.486
And now, after collecting the tomatoes at Nuno's farm,
and after a long week of work...

00:25:01.486 --> 00:25:04.200
We can&nbsp;enjoy this tomato sauce at pizza night.

00:25:28.837 --> 00:25:30.642
Alright! That was it for this update!

00:25:30.642 --> 00:25:35.533
If you&nbsp;already want to watch the next update,
you can support us on Patreon.

00:25:35.533 --> 00:25:37.794
If not, you&nbsp;can see us next week.

00:25:37.794 --> 00:25:39.416
Same time, same day!

00:25:39.416 --> 00:25:40.365
Ciao!

